# Direct calls to Statistics Denmark, for comparing GET and POST.
# Both return the same CSV. The service itself uses POST, as described in the assignment.

### GET: the whole query in the URL ("Ø" in LØNSUM must be URL-encoded as %C3%98)
GET https://api.statbank.dk/v1/data/ERHV1/CSV?valuePresentation=Code&BRANCHE07=212000&TAL=ARBSTED,ANSATTE,FULDBESK,L%C3%98NSUM&TID=2024

### POST: the same query as a JSON body (what StatbankClient sends)
POST https://api.statbank.dk/v1/data
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "table": "ERHV1",
  "format": "CSV",
  "valuePresentation": "Code",
  "variables": [
    { "code": "BRANCHE07", "values": ["212000"] },
    { "code": "TAL", "values": ["ARBSTED", "ANSATTE", "FULDBESK", "LØNSUM"] },
    { "code": "TID", "values": ["2024"] }
  ]
}

### Unknown industry code (new DB25 code) -> 400 EXTRACT-NOTFOUND
POST https://api.statbank.dk/v1/data
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "table": "ERHV1",
  "format": "CSV",
  "valuePresentation": "Code",
  "variables": [
    { "code": "BRANCHE07", "values": ["471200"] },
    { "code": "TAL", "values": ["ARBSTED"] },
    { "code": "TID", "values": ["2024"] }
  ]
}

# Calls to the service running in Docker on port 8080.
# Start it with "docker build -t company-enrichment ." and "docker run --rm -p 8080:8080 company-enrichment".

### Lookup by CVR number (Novo Nordisk) -> company data and industry statistics in one response
GET http://localhost:8080/api/companies/24256790?year=2024

### Metrics in Prometheus format (response time and status codes for the service, CVR and Statistics Denmark)
# Send a few requests first, otherwise there is nothing to show
GET http://localhost:8080/metrics